 From: Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
To: Constructed Languages List <CONLANG@listserv.brown.edu>; International Auxiliary Languages <AUXLANG@listserv.brown.edu>; lojban@googlegroups.com 
Sent: Tuesday, April 1, 2014 2:45 AM
Subject: [lojban] The Voynich manuscript. A new study. Written in Lojban?
 


The researchers from the University of Laguna Verde are reporting that they have made a new breakthrough in deciphering The Voynich Manuscript.

The study pointed out the fact that the language of the manuscript couldn't be a normal human language due to the clearly seen low entropy of the text.

The article hasn't been published yet but the authors kindly provided me with the draft of their paper that very soon will be published in Laguna Verde University proceedings.

http://mw.lojban.org/files/docs/voynich.pdf


This might sound strange but they came to conclusion that the manuscript was written in a variation of the logical language Lojban.


Several words from the manuscript have been translated after a laborious digitalizing of the manuscript and careful analysis of the pictures, history of Mediaeval Italy and advances in modern logical science.
